    "text": "Thread the darning needle with about 40 cm of matching dark green wool darning yarn, single strand, no knot. On the wrong side, anchor in solid knit about 8 mm outside the largest hole with 2 tiny backstitches in the knit loops. Goal is visible: yarn is fixed and will not pull through.",
    "common_mistake": "Do not use a long thread over 50 cm - it tangles and weakens the wool yarn.",
